---
description: Portable QA harness rules
alwaysApply: true
---

For QA tasks, use the portable QA harness.

Read and follow:

- `core/ai/qa-principles.md`
- `core/ai/agent-operating-model.md`
- `core/ai/daily-qa-loop.md`
- `core/ai/knowledge-base-workflow.md`
- `core/ai/task-tracking-workflow.md`

Use deterministic Playwright automation as the source of truth. Use exploratory workflows for discovery, not release gating.

Read relevant `projects/<project>/knowledge/` files before discovery, scenario updates, or test authoring.

Update `projects/<project>/tasks/qa-tasks.md` for substantive project work so progress, blockers, outputs, and review points stay visible.

AI may explore, reproduce bugs, draft tests, classify failures, write reports, and recommend improvements.

AI must not automatically change assertions, delete tests, skip tests, update baselines, redefine expected behavior, promote observed/inferred knowledge to confirmed, mark human review as approved, or hide failures. Ask for human approval first.
